According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Aerospace Fasteners market was valued at USD 7 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 10 billion by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 3.8% during the forecast period (2026–2034). This growth is driven by rising aircraft production volumes, increasing demand for lightweight yet high strength connections, and tightening regulatory requirements that favor premium, traceable fastener solutions.
Aerospace fasteners comprise high precision bolts, screws, nuts, rivets and washers that secure structural panels, engine components and interior systems on both commercial and defense aircraft. These parts are fabricated from lightweight alloys such as titanium, aluminum lithium and high strength steel, often featuring corrosion resistant coatings. Because aircraft operate under extreme temperature cycles, vibration loads and strict safety standards, fasteners are engineered for fatigue resistance, dimensional stability and full compliance with aviation quality systems such as AS9100.
